          "literatureReview": "A Complete Blood Count (CBC) is a fundamental blood test that provides essential information about the types and numbers of cells in the blood, including red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets. It is commonly used to assess overall health, diagnose various conditions such as anemia, infections, and many other disorders. The CBC test can help detect abnormalities in blood cell counts and provide insights into a patient's immune system and oxygen-carrying capacity."
